Subject: [PATCH RFC 0/3] media: i2c: dw9719: optional VDDIO on SP11 OLED

This incremental series adds the rear DW9800K actuator and its
shared power management to Oaklee's tested OV13858 rear camera
enablement for Surface Pro 11 OLED.

Exact baseline: Oaklee 52812090bd341a2a1e609f32afa4595b51a97127
with the earlier, already-shared rear-camera board patch applied.
The CAMSS/PHY changes from the previous November 20 handover
must be present as appropriate; do not reapply duplicates.

The lens uses PM8550 L16B 2.912 V as VDD but also requires
PM8010 L6M 1.8 V I/O, shared with sensor DOVDD. The driver
maintains a separate, optional regulator vote; DTS connects
the sensor's lens-focus to DW9800K at CCI0 master1 0x0c.

Tested on the physical SP11 with Oaklee kernel
7.3.0-jg-1sp11v15-qcom-x1e and isolated Ubuntu userspace:
- actuator probe and focus controls succeeded;
- shared L6M votes followed 0/1/2/1/0 during open/close;
- rear 120/120 4224x3136 RAW frames around 29.95 fps;
- direct 240-frame capture continued across VCM open/close;
- front IMX681 30/30 and IR VD55G0 60/60 RAW frames passed;
- three device-PM callback cycles each followed by focus and
  a 30-frame rear capture succeeded, with zero PM failures.

The tested boot changed only a copy of the OLED DTB payload
inside the previously qualified Oaklee EFI image; a production
kernel/DTB build must use the normal build process. Neither real
deep standby nor optical lens sharpness has been verified.

The series is three patches numbered 0004..0006 in the handover
ZIP to distinguish it from the previous 0001..0003 assistance.
See README-START-HERE.md and evidence/.

